Applicable Role: Hardware Engineers, PCB Quality Inspection, Procurement & Manufacturing Teams

---
📌 Overview
PCB acceptance standards are the core "technical yardstick" for hardware design, factory inspection and mass production quality control in electronic projects.
In domestic and overseas electronic manufacturing scenarios, three standard systems are widely used, with clear positioning differences:
- IPC: Global universal industry baseline standard (international mainstream)
- GB/T: Chinese national recommended standard (civilian domestic scenarios)
- GJB: Chinese military high-reliability mandatory standard (defense, aerospace and high-end reliable equipment)
This document systematically sorts out the grading rules, core technical indicators, scenario differences and cross-standard mapping relationships of the three systems, providing a direct reference for engineers to select standards and verify PCB acceptance.

---
🌍 IPC International Standard System
IPC is the dominant international standard for electronic assembly and PCB manufacturing, adopted globally by North America, Europe and APAC electronics industries. It covers full-process workmanship, performance and reliability verification.
Core Standard Series
- IPC-A-600: PCB visual appearance workmanship acceptance specification
- IPC-6010 Series: PCB performance and reliability qualification specifications
IPC 3-Level Reliability Classification
IPC adopts a mature hierarchical system based on product application scenarios and reliability requirements:
- Class 1 | Consumer Grade
Applicable to toys, daily appliances and ordinary consumer electronics. Focus on basic functional availability; minor cosmetic defects are allowable.
- Class 2 | Industrial Grade
Applicable to industrial control, communication equipment, commercial vehicle electronics. Require stable long-term operation; allowable extremely limited downtime.
- Class 3 | High-Reliability Grade
Applicable to aerospace, medical equipment, key automotive electronic hardware. Require zero interruption under harsh working conditions, full inspection coverage.
Supplement: IPC-6012DS 3A (unofficial Class 4) is for space-grade avionics, with ultra-strict process and performance requirements and high manufacturing costs.
Key IPC Technical Indicators
- Barrel copper thickness: Class 2 average ≥20μm; Class 3 average ≥25μm
- Thermal stress test: Class 2 completes 3 cycles @288℃/10s; Class 3 ≥3 cycles
- Inspection requirement: Class 3 mandatory 100% electrical test + full inspection of key dimensions

