🛡️ GJB Chinese Military Standard System
GJB is the mandatory military standard for China’s defense and aerospace electronic equipment, oriented to high-reliability and extreme working condition scenarios. Its technical system is aligned with the US military standards MIL-PRF-31032 / MIL-PRF-55110.
Core applicable specification: GJB 362B-2009 (Rigid Printed Circuit Board General Specification)
GJB Grade & IPC Class Mapping
- GJB Grade Ⅰ ≈ IPC Class 1: General equipment, service life 5-10 years
- GJB Grade Ⅱ ≈ IPC Class 2: Industrial communication equipment, service life >10 years
- GJB Grade Ⅲ ≫ IPC Class 3: Military and aerospace core equipment, service life >15 years
Key Difference: GJB Grade 3 is far stricter than ordinary IPC Class 3 in environmental adaptability, batch consistency and full-process traceability.
Unique Mandatory Military Test Items
In addition to conventional electrical and dimensional inspection, GJB mandatory adds extreme environment and reliability verification:
- Salt spray corrosion test, solvent resistance test
- High and low temperature damp-heat cycle test
- Vibration shock test, thermal shock test (-55℃ ~ +125℃)
- Electromigration reliability test
Meanwhile, full-process production traceability and GJB 9001 military quality system certification are mandatory for manufacturers.

---
🇨🇳 GB/T Chinese Recommended National Standard
The GB/T series is a domestic recommended national standard for civilian PCB manufacturing, referenced from IEC and IPC international standards, suitable for ordinary domestic civilian electronic projects.
Core Features
- No unified reliability grading system like IPC/GJB; classified by board type (single-sided, double-sided, multilayer)
- Overall acceptance level is equivalent to IPC Class 1~2, insufficient for high-reliability and military scenarios
- High-end domestic projects generally adopt IPC or GJB standards directly
Important Update: GB/T 4588.1/.2-1996 was officially withdrawn in July 2026, replaced by the new version GB/T 4588-2025

